    "# Hotel Reservations Agent with AgentCore and PostgreSQL\n",
    "\n",
    "## Overview\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook demonstrates how to build a sophisticated hotel reservation system using Amazon Bedrock AgentCore with the Strands framework and PostgreSQL database. Unlike the original lab with hardcoded values, this implementation uses a real database with synthetic data for 10 hotels, each with 5 rooms.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Features\n",
    "- **Hotel Search**: Find hotels by location, rating, and price\n",
    "- **Room Availability**: Check real-time availability for specific dates\n",
    "- **Reservations**: Complete booking process with guest information\n",
    "- **Booking Management**: Look up and cancel existing reservations\n",
    "- **PostgreSQL Integration**: Persistent data storage with proper relationships\n",
    "\n",
    "### Architecture\n",
    "- **AgentCore with Strands**: AI agent framework\n",
    "- **Amazon Bedrock**: Claude 3.7 Sonnet model\n",
    "- **PostgreSQL**: Database with hotels, rooms, and reservations\n",
    "- **Custom Tools**: Specialized functions for hotel operations"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
